# Schema geo

Geo reference vocabulary for county-level records.

## Class Diagram

```mermaid
classDiagram
    direction TB
    class State {
        code String
    }
    class District {
        <<Part>>
        id UUID
    }
    class County {
        fips FipsCode
        population Integer
    }
    County --> State : IN_STATE (one)
    County *-- District : HAS_DISTRICT (many)
```

## Types

### State

State is a US state.

| Property | Type | Modifiers | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `code` | `String` | primary |  |

### District

*Part type* — instances exist only as composed children.

| Property | Type | Modifiers | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | `UUID` | primary |  |

### County

County is a US county node.

| Property | Type | Modifiers | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `fips` | `FipsCode` | primary |  |
| `population` | `Integer` | required | population is the resident count at the last census. |

**Associations**

- `--> IN_STATE (one)` [State](#state)

  IN_STATE records the county's state.

**Compositions**

- `*-> HAS_DISTRICT (many)` [District](#district)

  HAS_DISTRICT holds electoral districts.

## Data Types

| Name | Definition | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `FipsCode` | `String[5, 5]` | FipsCode is a five-character FIPS identifier. |
